ck (beating Q, 10, etc.), and if beaten by A or 2, that’s acceptable because those are high commitments from the opponent.\n\nAlternatively, leading ♠A guarantees winning the trick, giving me control to continue playing, which could help set up my teammate. With only three cards left, gaining immediate control allows me to potentially run through my hand quickly, especially if my teammate is also low on cards.\n\nReason: Leading ♠A ensures I win the trick and retain initiative. This allows me to immediately follow up on my next turn with whatever I have left, possibly clearing my hand before the landlord. Given that both peasants still have around 10 cards each, coordination isn\'t obvious, but taking control now increases pressure on the landlord. Passing isn\'t allowed (free play), so I must lead. Among the singles, ♠A gives maximum control.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠A"]}'}
